  "surprise": "P33/P37 learned per-block ALiBi slopes (24 log-space params, init 1/4, 1/16, 1/64, 1/256 in every block, no pretraining decay, NoPE heads fixed at 0; 4,800,024 params; cached vs full forward max logit diff 8.6e-7 on CPU) on 115-fable scored 623/633/647 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115's 639/646/609: exact means 634.33 vs 631.33, +3.0, paired -16/-13/+38, inside the registered -40..+35 range (central 0). Discard under the simplicity rule although the mean is strictly above: an improvement of ~0 (about 0.1 sd of a 3-seed mean, two of three seeds lower) that adds a 20-line patch, 24 free parameters and a ~9% pretraining step cost; this matches 116-fable's discard of the unconstrained version (T5-bucketed table) at the identical 634.33. The registered mechanism is NOT supported: round-1 targets solved 698/738/667 vs 115's 718/756/691 (lower on every seed, -20/-18/-24), round-1 sample acc 0.298/0.339/0.265 vs 0.318/0.301/0.315, round-1 parse failures 9880/9321/15970 of 48,000 (21/19/33%) vs 25/22/18%, so the start did not get cleaner. RL then climbed slightly more (r4 1113/1119/1131, mean 1121 vs 1106; r1->r4 +415/+381/+464) but the eval frontier did not move: ge10 90/89/105 vs 103/97/89, ge11 18/17/22 vs 25/23/19, ge12 4/5/4 vs 5/4/4, L* 11/12/11, eval parse failures 12837/11903/13157 of 70,912 vs 11563/11640/13004. Learned slopes at handoff (surprise: they barely moved, at most a factor 1.6 from init, with the same depth pattern on all three seeds): head 1 (init 1/4) steepened to 1/2.4-1/2.95 in blocks 0-1 and stayed 1/3.2-1/4.3 in blocks 2-5; head 2 (1/16) went to 1/11.0-1/14.0 in blocks 0-1 and 1/15.2-1/18.5 in blocks 3-5; heads 3-4 stayed within about 20% of 1/64 and 1/256 with no depth pattern. So pretraining asks for a mild P37 gradient (lower blocks more local), not a different table, and the fixed 115 table was already near what cap-6 data wants. Slopes also kept training under the harness RL AdamW; post-RL values were not logged. Cost: 3853/3766/3887 pretraining steps vs 4204/4218/4263 (-8.3/-10.7/-8.8%, just below the predicted -8..+2%), half of 116-fable's -18%, consistent with its diagnosis that SDPA leaves the fused kernel once attn_mask requires grad. The lost steps cost no fit: final val loss 0.0845/0.0840/0.0841 vs 0.0826/0.0806/0.0792 (minima 0.0769/0.0795/0.0756 vs 0.0778/0.0793/0.0777, all rising into the endpoint), held-out greedy 0.982/0.984/0.979 vs 0.9815/0.983/0.9845, eval greedy 0.989/0.989/0.9915. Totals 1681/1588/1842 s (seed 2 on a slow pod: 188-205 samples/s in rounds 2-4). Follow-up if anyone wants the depth pattern: freeze it as a fixed per-block table (blocks 0-1 head 1 at 1/2.7, head 2 at 1/12.5), which needs no mask gradient and so costs no steps.",
